  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Moves fighter $99 by the step in byte 10 of the pose record. Byte 9 holds the direction bits. The facing swaps the bits (EOR $7f48). Bit 2: X decreases. Bit 3: X increases. Fighters that pass each other move back."},
    {"at":28,"placement":"side","text":"Bit 2 into carry."},
    {"at":65,"placement":"line","text":"Decreases $71,x by $ae. Minimum: 3 when the fighter faces right ($91,x = 0), else 0."},
    {"at":98,"placement":"line","text":"Increases $71,x by $ae. Maximum: $1c. When the fighter faces right, only a value of $20 or more becomes $1c."},
    {"at":125,"placement":"line","text":"Calculates the gap between the fighters from the facing of fighter 0 into $c3. Negative: the fighters passed each other. When fighter X does move $91 and the other fighter does move $84, it sets $b2 = $84 (turn request). Output: A = gap, N set only for a negative gap that must be corrected. After a beaten fighter ($af bit 7), N is clear."}
  ],
